{
  "title": "Extract a shared recipe-version write service (new-version \
transaction copy-pasted across 5 handlers)",
  "description": "The core mutation of the app — insert a new recipe_versions \
row, repoint recipes.current_version_id, and carry tags forward — is \
reimplemented inline in five API handlers:\n\
\n\
- server/src/api/recipes/create.rs:85-140\n\
- server/src/api/recipes/update.rs:224-270\n\
- server/src/api/recipes/normalize_title.rs:195-249\n\
- server/src/api/recipes/generate_description.rs:~221-255\n\
- server/src/api/recipes/generate_photo.rs:352-386\n\
\n\
A helper copy_recipe_version_tags already exists at \
server/src/scraping/steps.rs:628 and is used by the pipeline, but the API \
handlers each re-hand-roll the same old_tag_ids load + on_conflict_do_nothing \
insert loop (normalize_title.rs:233-245, generate_description.rs:243-254, \
generate_photo.rs:373-386). This is the most dangerous duplication in the \
codebase: a missed tag-copy or a divergent transaction in one handler silently \
corrupts user data.\n\
\n\
Fix: introduce a recipes service module (e.g. create_recipe and \
create_new_version(conn, recipe_id, NewRecipeVersion, tag_source)), move \
copy_recipe_version_tags and the tag-upsert loop there, and have all five \
handlers (and the pipeline steps) call it. Server-side only — no client \
changes, no `make pipeline` data/ diffs expected (behavior-preserving \
refactor).",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 2,
  "type": "task",
  "labels": [
    "api",
    "architecture",
  ],
